{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LoK7F5Ptu1G5yfeCMgEuEH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for the \"worst\" tier scenario, based on the experiment plan defined in the project context. Let me carefully analyze each planned experiment and produce worst-case predictions consistent with the worst tier definition.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n- Classification advantage negligible (gap ≤4 F1 points vs CWM generation)\n- Per-test signal mostly redundant with trajectory-level\n- Story collapses to analysis paper\n\nKey metric ranges for worst:\n- cwm_generation_per_class_f1: [83, 87]\n\n\n- classification_minus_cwm_gap: [0, 4]\n- trace_then_judge_f1: [84, 88]\n- repo_level_per_class_f1: [55, 69]\n- diagnostic_rerepair_resolve_lift_pct: [0, 1]\n- block_corr_spearman_vs_iid: [0.0, 0.1]\n- per_test_failure_precision: [0.65, 0.75]\n- per_test_failure_recall: [0.6, 0.7]\n\nThe core assumption here is that CWM generation performs comparably to classification, with minimal gains from the per-test diagnostic approach, and the block-level correlation signal is essentially noise.\n\nNow I'm working through the worst-case predictions for each planned experiment, starting with the ones already completed—the oracle simulation, data prep, and training runs all came back as expected, with the regression rate showing negative results. I need to map out predictions for the remaining experiments, beginning with the CWM baseline.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10118,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10118},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"843dc94