{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LoK7F5Ptu1G5yfeCMgEuEH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 失败——CWM generation 在 function-level 4B 规模上与 classification 差距 ≤4 F1，\n  Trace-then-Judge 进一步证明 classification formulation 并非关键因素。\n  Claim 2 失败——per-test 诊断精度不足以驱动有效 re-repair，lift 接近零。\n  Claim 3 的 oracle frontier 成为唯一可回收贡献，但 block correlation 实证不支持，\n  per-test 优势仅在 iid+高 T 条件下理论存在，SWE-bench 分布不满足。\n  论文重构为 analysis/negative-result paper:\n  \"Do We Need Per-Test Execution Simulation? An Empirical Investigation\"，\n  投 ICSE 2027 empirical study track 或 EMNLP Findings (reframe 为 probing LLM code reasoning)。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"CWM Generation Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"cwm-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 CWM generation（预测 execution output），\n      与 classification model (87.1/87.9 F1) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      cwm_generation_pass_f1: 84.3\n      cwm_generation_fail_f1: 85.1\n      cwm_generation_overall_accuracy: 0.847\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_pass_f1: 2.8\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_fail_f1: 2.8\n      cwm_token_budget_overflow_rate: 0.03\n      cwm_exact_match_rate: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      Function-level test 的 expected output 通常很短（单个返回值、True/False、短字符串），\n      token-budget exhaustion 在 CWM debugging 论文中报告的问题主要出现在 repo-level 长 trace 场景。\n      4B 模型在 function-level 生成短输出时不会遇到严重的 token 限制，\n      string-value prediction error 也因输出简单而低频（overflow rate ~3%）。\n      因此 generation 与 classification 的差距被压缩到 ≤4 F1 点，\n      说明 \"task reformulation\" 的优势在 function-level 尺度上不显著——\n      classification 之所以更好，仅仅是因为输出空间更小，而非根本性的 formulation 优势。\n      exact match ~61% 看似不高，但 pass/fail 判定只需对 output 做二值判断，\n      大部分 non-exact-match 的 output 仍能正确推导出 pass/fail 结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Classification vs CWM Generation (Qwen3-4B, function-level)\"\n        columns: [Model, Formulation, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Accuracy, Token_Overflow_Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B-LoRA, Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 0.875, \"N/A\"]\n          - [Qwen3-4B-LoRA, \"CWM Generation\", 84.3, 85.1, 0.847, 0.03]\n          - [Delta, \"\", -2.8, -2.8, -0.028, \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-class F1 bar chart: classification vs generation, 误差棒重叠显著，gap 不具统计显著性 (p>0.05, bootstrap CI)\"\n    analysis: >\n      2.8 F1 的差距在统计上不显著（bootstrap 95% CI 横跨零点）。\n      function-level output 足够短，generation 不遭遇 CWM 论文中的 token-budget 瓶颈。\n      这意味着 \"reformulation from generation to classification\" 的叙事在 function-level 不成立——\n      classification 仅是 marginally better，无法支撑 Claim 1 的核心论点。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B/8B 先生成 execution trace，再从 trace 中抽取 pass/fail。\n      隔离 classification advantage 是来自 formulation（不需要 trace）还是 task simplicity。\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_4b_pass_f1: 85.2\n      ttj_4b_fail_f1: 85.9\n      ttj_8b_pass_f1: 87.8\n      ttj_8b_fail_f1: 88.4\n      ttj_4b_vs_direct_classification_gap: -1.9\n      ttj_8b_vs_direct_classification_gap: 0.7\n      trace_generation_accuracy: 0.78\n      trace_to_verdict_accuracy_given_correct_trace: 0.97\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 在 4B 时略低于 direct classification（-1.9 F1），\n      但在 8B 时反超（+0.7 F1）。这说明 trace generation 确实提供了中间推理步骤的价值，\n      只是 4B 模型容量不足以同时 generate trace 并做 judgment。\n      8B 反超意味着 classification formulation 的优势不是根本性的，\n      而仅仅是 4B 规模下的 capacity 约束造成的——\n      给足参数后，generation + extraction 方案同样有效甚至更好。\n      这直接摧毁了 \"classification is fundamentally simpler\" 的论点：\n      它只是对小模型更友好，不是一个 formulation-level insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification\"\n        columns: [Model, Method, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Avg_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Direct Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5]\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Trace-then-Judge, 85.2, 85.9, 85.6]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Direct Classification, 89.4, 90.1, 89.8]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Trace-then-Judge, 87.8, 88.4, 88.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4B vs 8B 两组对比图，8B 组中 Trace-then-Judge 与 Direct Classification 的 CI 完全重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      TTJ 8B 与 direct classification 8B 差距 <2 F1，且 TTJ 8B 与 direct classification 4B 性能相当。\n      这表明 trace generation 不是瓶颈——模型规模才是。\n      Claim 1 的 \"formulation matters\" 论点被 confound 于 model capacity，无法独立成立。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-level Finetuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved 分类器，\n      隔离 granularity effect vs formulation effect。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_level_accuracy: 0.852\n      traj_level_resolved_f1: 84.8\n      traj_level_unresolved_f1: 85.5\n      per_test_aggregated_to_traj_accuracy: 0.861\n      per_test_vs_traj_level_gap: 0.9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level finetuned 模型直接从 (code, full_test_suite) 预测 resolved/unresolved，\n      不需要 per-test 中间步骤。在 T=1 dominant (68.7%) 的分布下，\n      trajectory-level 与 per-test-then-aggregate 的信息量几乎等价。\n      差距仅 0.9 ppt 说明 per-test granularity 在当前 benchmark 分布下\n      几乎不提供额外信息——aggregation 的理论优势被 T=1 dominance 抹平。\n      少量 T≥2 instances 上 per-test 有优势，但被 T=1 的等价性稀释。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-test Aggregated vs Trajectory-level (Qwen3-4B)\"\n        columns: [Granularity, Accuracy, Resolved_F1, Unresolved_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Per-test → Aggregate, 0.861, 85.7, 86.4]\n          - [Trajectory-level Direct, 0.852, 84.8, 85.5]\n          - [Delta, +0.009, +0.9, +0.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy 对比柱状图，差异在 error bar 内不显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test → aggregate 方法比 trajectory-level 仅高 0.9 ppt，\n      在 bootstrap test 下 p=0.18，不显著。\n      对于 68.7% 的 T=1 instances 而言两种方法数学等价，\n      per-test granularity 的优势仅在 T≥2 的 31.3% 子集上可能体现，\n      但被整体 accuracy 稀释到不可区分。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B→8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM generation 分别 scale 到 8B，\n      观察 classification advantage 是否随规模保持。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_8b_pass_f1: 89.4\n      classification_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cwm_generation_8b_pass_f1: 88.1\n      cwm_generation_8b_fail_f1: 88.7\n      gap_8b: 1.3\n      gap_4b: 2.8\n      gap_trend: \"narrowing\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 规模下 CWM generation 进一步逼近 classification（gap 从 2.8 缩小到 1.3）。\n      更大模型的 generation capacity 提升更快——\n      generation 的难度主要来自需要\"记住\"输出格式和预测具体值，\n      这些随参数量增加而快速改善。\n      Classification 的提升相对 moderate 因为 4B 已接近 function-level 的 ceiling。\n      gap narrowing 趋势进一步削弱 \"formulation advantage\" 论点——\n      如果差距随 scale 消失，那 classification 只是小模型的 regularization effect，\n      不是一个 scale-invariant insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Classification vs Generation across Model Sizes\"\n        columns: [Size, Classification_Avg_F1, Generation_Avg_F1, Gap]\n        rows:\n          - [4B, 87.5, 84.7, 2.8]\n          - [8B, 89.8, 88.4, 1.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scaling curve: x=model size, y=avg F1, 两条线收敛\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 从 4B 的 2.8 缩小到 8B 的 1.3，趋势线外推到 ~14B 处交叉。\n      这意味着 classification advantage 是 small-model phenomenon，\n      不是一个 fundamental formulation insight。\n      论文若以此为 main claim 将面临 \"just use a bigger model\" 的 reviewer 质疑。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      200 instances 上比较：repair agent 使用 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，\n      衡量 resolve rate lift。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 0.34\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.345\n      resolve_rate_lift_pct: 0.5\n      diagnostic_precision_at_threshold: 0.69\n      actionable_diagnostic_rate: 0.23\n    result_rationale: >\n      Diagnostic re-repair 要求两个条件同时满足：(1) per-test prediction 足够准确以识别 failing test，\n      (2) repair agent 能利用 \"test X fails\" 信息生成 targeted fix。\n      在 worst 档位下，per-test failure precision 仅 0.69，意味着 ~31% 的诊断指向是错误的，\n      给 repair agent 引入噪声反而可能 mislead。\n      此外，即使诊断正确，repair agent 可能已经从 error message 中获得等价信息，\n      使得 per-test prediction 的边际信息量很低。\n      0.5% lift 在 200 instances 上对应 ~1 个额外 resolved instance，\n      远低于统计显著性门槛。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Resolve Rates\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve_Rate, N_Resolved, Lift]\n        rows:\n          - [No diagnostic, 0.340, \"68/200\", \"—\"]\n          - [With per-test diagnostic, 0.345, \"69/200\", \"+0.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Resolve rate 柱状图，error bar 完全重叠\"\n      - \"Error analysis: 诊断正确且 repair 成功 vs 诊断错误且 mislead 的 case breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      0.5% lift 不显著（Fisher exact test p=0.91）。\n      定性分析显示：诊断正确的 cases 中，repair agent 在无诊断条件下也多数能 resolve（从 error trace 获得等价信息）；\n      诊断错误的 cases 中，misleading 信息反而导致 repair agent 走偏。\n      净效果接近零。Claim 2 不成立。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Failure Precision/Recall\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall。\n    expected_results:\n      per_test_failure_precision: 0.71\n      per_test_failure_recall: 0.65\n      per_test_failure_f1: 0.679\n      per_test_pass_precision: 0.89\n      per_test_pass_recall: 0.92\n      false_positive_rate: 0.08\n      false_negative_rate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Failure 是少数类（~35% of test outcomes in training data），precision/recall 偏低是预期的。\n      模型对 PASS 的预测更可靠（recall 0.92）因为 PASS 是多数类且模式更 regular。\n      FAIL prediction 的 35% false negative rate 意味着模型漏掉了 1/3 的真实 failure，\n      这直接限制了 diagnostic signal 的下游可用性——\n      如果你只能捕获 65% 的 failing tests，剩余 35% 的遗漏会让 repair agent \n      以为某些 test 是通过的（实际未通过），产生 false confidence。\n      71% precision 意味着每指出的 ~3.5 个 failing test 中有 1 个是误报。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-test Prediction Quality\"\n        columns: [Label, Precision, Recall, F1, Support]\n        rows:\n          - [PASS, 0.89, 0.92, 0.905, \"~6500\"]\n          - [FAIL, 0.71, 0.65, 0.679, \"~3500\"]\n          - [Macro Avg, 0.80, 0.785, 0.792, \"~10000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for FAIL class，AUC-PR ~0.72\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap\"\n    analysis: >\n      FAIL class 的 F1=0.679 处于 worst 定义范围内。\n      与 overall accuracy 0.875 的落差说明 class imbalance 下 per-test failure detection 困难。\n      这个精度水平不足以支撑可靠的 diagnostic feedback——\n      下游 re-repair 实验中 0.5% lift 的结果与此一致。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T=3+) 分层的 oracle advantage 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct: 0.687\n      T1_iid_adv: 0.0\n      T1_block_adv: 0.0\n      T2_pct: 0.158\n      T2_iid_adv: 0.042\n      T2_block_adv: 0.118\n      T3plus_pct: 0.155\n      T3plus_iid_adv: 0.185\n      T3plus_block_adv: 0.362\n      weighted_avg_iid_adv: 0.035\n      weighted_avg_block_adv: 0.075\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=1 时 per-test 与 trajectory-level 数学等价（advantage = 0）。\n      T=2 时 iid advantage 仅 0.042 因为两个独立 coin flips 的组合增益很小。\n      T=3+ 时 advantage 显著（iid 0.185, block 0.362），但仅占 15.5% instances。\n      加权平均后 iid advantage 仅 0.035, block 仅 0.075——\n      在 worst 档下 block correlation 未被实证支持，\n      所以实际 expected advantage 接近 iid 的 0.035，\n      即 per-test 在当前 SWE-bench 分布下仅贡献 ~3.5 ppt 的 oracle advantage。\n      这个 3.5 ppt 还是 oracle 上界——实际模型的 advantage 会更小。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Oracle Per-test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [T_stratum, Instance_Pct, iid_Advantage, Block_Advantage]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", 0.000, 0.000]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"15.8%\", 0.042, 0.118]\n          - [\"T=3+\", \"15.5%\", 0.185, 0.362]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", 0.035, 0.075]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: T 分层分布 + 各层 advantage overlay\"\n      - \"Advantage vs T 曲线，标注 SWE-bench T 分布的 CDF\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test advantage 高度集中在 T≥3（仅 15.5% instances），\n      但 SWE-bench 的 T=1 dominance (68.7%) 使加权 advantage 骤降。\n      这是 Claim 3 的核心可回收发现：per-test verification 有价值的严格前提条件\n      在当前主流 benchmark 上不被满足。\n      作为 analysis paper 的贡献有说服力，但作为 method paper 的 motivation 不够。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练模型的 test-level predictions 中测量实际 error correlation 结构，\n      与 iid 和 block-correlated simulation 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_corr_within_instance: 0.06\n      iid_simulation_spearman: 0.02\n      block_simulation_spearman: 0.45\n      observed_closer_to: \"iid\"\n      kendall_tau: 0.04\n      avg_error_cluster_size: 1.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Block correlation 假设（同一 instance 内所有 test 的 prediction error 高度相关）\n      基于直觉：如果模型不理解 patch 的语义，所有 test 都会预测错误。\n      但实际上 4B 模型的错误更 heterogeneous——\n      有些 test 因为 input/output pattern 简单而容易预测正确，\n      即使模型对 patch 语义理解不完整。\n      Spearman 0.06 接近 iid 基线 (0.02) 而远离 block 模拟 (0.45)，\n      说明 errors 近似独立。\n      这意味着 oracle analysis 中 block-correlated 列的数字不适用于实际模型，\n      per-test advantage 应参考 iid 列——进一步缩小 advantage。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [Model, Spearman_ρ, Kendall_τ, Avg_Error_Cluster]\n        rows:\n          - [Observed (Qwen3-4B), 0.06, 0.04, 1.2]\n          - [iid Simulation, 0.02, 0.01, 1.05]\n          - [Block Simulation, 0.45, 0.38, 3.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error correlation heatmap: instances × tests，显示 near-random pattern\"\n      - \"Q-Q plot: observed correlation distribution vs iid null distribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      Observed Spearman ρ=0.06，远低于 block simulation (0.45)，\n      仅略高于 iid (0.02)。KS test 无法拒绝 iid null (p=0.23)。\n      Block correlation assumption 不成立。\n      Oracle analysis 中的 block advantage 列 (0.075 weighted) 不适用，\n      实际应参考 iid advantage 列 (0.035 weighted)。\n      Per-test 的理论优势进一步缩水。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重新评估 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_instances: 412\n      docker_failure_rate: 0.176\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 47.3\n      avg_f2p_tests: 2.1\n      avg_p2p_tests: 45.2\n      total_test_examples: 311072\n      p2p_regression_rate: 0.013\n    result_rationale: >\n      Docker 评估的 ~17.6% 失败率来自环境配置不兼容（依赖版本、Python 版本等），\n      与 SWE-bench 官方 Docker 评估的已知问题一致。\n      412 instances × 16 candidates × avg 47.3 tests ≈ 311K test-level examples。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3% 与之前 p2p-regression-rate 实验结论一致（negative）。\n      这个数据集本身有资源贡献价值，但 per-test labels 在 worst 档下\n      无法驱动比 trajectory-level 显著更好的 verification。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Instances (successful), 412]\n          - [Candidates per instance, 16]\n          - [Avg total tests, 47.3]\n          - [Avg F2P tests, 2.1]\n          - [Avg P2P tests, 45.2]\n          - [P2P regression rate, \"1.3%\"]\n          - [Total test examples, \"~311K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"F2P test count 分布直方图，长尾但中位数=1\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功但统计特性与 function-level 类似：F2P 中位数=1，T=1 dominant。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3% 低于 oracle study 中 10% 阈值，\n      确认 P2P tests 在当前 benchmark 上不提供有用的 verification signal。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-level Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B/8B fine-tune on repo-level (patched_code, test_code) → pass/fail。\n    expected_results:\n      repo_4b_pass_f1: 62.1\n      repo_4b_fail_f1: 59.7\n      repo_4b_accuracy: 0.643\n      repo_8b_pass_f1: 67.3\n      repo_8b_fail_f1: 65.8\n      repo_8b_accuracy: 0.689\n      context_length_avg_tokens: 6200\n      context_truncation_rate: 0.31\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level test code 远长于 function-level（avg 6200 tokens vs ~800），\n      且 patched code 包含跨文件修改，语义复杂度远高于单函数。\n      4B 模型 context window 限制导致 31% instances 需要 truncation，\n      严重损害 prediction quality。\n      62/60 F1 远低于 function-level 的 87/88，\n      也低于 repo-level per_class_f1 worst 范围上界 69。\n      8B 通过更大 context capacity 部分缓解 truncation，\n      但 67/66 F1 仍不足以在实践中竞争 execution-based verification。\n      这个 accuracy 水平下的 per-test diagnostic 几乎无意义——\n      模型对 repo-level code 的理解不足以可靠区分 pass/fail。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Repo-level Classification Results\"\n        columns: [Model, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Accuracy, Truncation_Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B, 62.1, 59.7, 0.643, 0.31]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 67.3, 65.8, 0.689, 0.22]\n          - [\"Function-level 4B (ref)\", 87.1, 87.9, 0.875, 0.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Function-level vs Repo-level accuracy 对比，显示 >20 ppt gap\"\n      - \"Accuracy vs context length scatter，truncation 区域 accuracy 骤降\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level results 低于 70% F1 (worst 范围)，不具竞争力。\n      Function-level 到 repo-level 的 generalization gap 巨大（>20 ppt），\n      说明 per-test classification 的 function-level 成功不能外推到实际 SE 场景。\n      这强化了 analysis paper 的叙事：方法的适用条件很窄。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge (trajectory-level + per-test)。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_accuracy: 0.71\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_pass_f1: 74.2\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_fail_f1: 68.5\n      qwen3_32b_traj_accuracy: 0.78\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_pass_f1: 80.1\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_fail_f1: 76.3\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_vs_finetuned_4b_gap: -7.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 在 trajectory-level 上表现尚可（32B 达 78%），\n      但 per-test 精度低于 fine-tuned 4B classifier。\n      32B zero-shot per-test avg F1 78.2 vs fine-tuned 4B 87.5，差距 9.3 ppt——\n      说明 fine-tuning 仍有价值，但也表明 32B 的 zero-shot 能力已不差。\n      在 worst 档下这些 baseline 主要的意义是填充 Pareto frontier 图表，\n      显示 cost-accuracy tradeoff 的全貌。\n      但 32B zero-shot trajectory-level 78% 接近 fine-tuned 4B per-test 87.5%，\n      如果考虑 inference cost，zero-shot large model 是一个不错的 alternative——\n      这进一步削弱了 fine-tuned per-test classifier 的独立价值。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines vs Fine-tuned Classifier\"\n        columns: [Model, Method, Traj_Acc, PerTest_Pass_F1, PerTest_Fail_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Zero-shot, 0.71, 74.2, 68.5]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Zero-shot, 0.78, 80.1, 76.3]\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Fine-tuned, 0.875, 87.1, 87.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier: x=inference cost (FLOPs), y=accuracy，标注各 method\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B 在 Pareto frontier 上优于 zero-shot 32B（更低 cost，更高 accuracy），\n      但这是 fine-tuning vs zero-shot 的一般结论，不是 per-test formulation 的功劳。\n      32B zero-shot trajectory-level 已接近 practical utility threshold。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Classification model 的 per-test majority voting (K=3)。\n    expected_results:\n      k1_pass_f1: 87.1\n      k1_fail_f1: 87.9\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      k3_fail_f1: 88.9\n      k3_lift: 1.1\n      k3_inference_cost_multiplier: 3.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      K=3 majority voting 提供 ~1.1 F1 的 lift，符合 self-consistency 的一般收益规律。\n      但 3x inference cost 换取 1.1 ppt 的 cost-effectiveness 很差。\n      在 worst 档下这个实验主要显示 per-test classification 已接近 \n      function-level 的 accuracy ceiling，additional inference budget 的 marginal return 递减。\n      不改变任何 main claim 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Majority Voting Results (K=3)\"\n        columns: [K, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Cost_Multiplier]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 87.1, 87.9, \"1x\"]\n          - [3, 88.3, 88.9, \"3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K vs F1 曲线，快速饱和\"\n    analysis: >\n      Low-impact experiment。1.1 ppt lift 不改变 worst 档的整体 narrative。\n      可放入 appendix 作为 completeness，不需要在 main paper 中讨论。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10118,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10118},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"843dc94e-0769-44b6-9749-612cb0b86756","uuid":"538ce0b8-5bd4-4223-8fba-2387432b3ace"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":186742,"duration_api_ms":188152,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 失败——CWM generation 在 function-level 4B 规模上与 classification 差距 ≤4 F1，\n  Trace-then-Judge 进一步证明 classification formulation 并非关键因素。\n  Claim 2 失败——per-test 诊断精度不足以驱动有效 re-repair，lift 接近零。\n  Claim 3 的 oracle frontier 成为唯一可回收贡献，但 block correlation 实证不支持，\n  per-test 优势仅在 iid+高 T 条件下理论存在，SWE-bench 分布不满足。\n  论文重构为 analysis/negative-result paper:\n  \"Do We Need Per-Test Execution Simulation? An Empirical Investigation\"，\n  投 ICSE 2027 empirical study track 或 EMNLP Findings (reframe 为 probing LLM code reasoning)。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"CWM Generation Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"cwm-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 CWM generation（预测 execution output），\n      与 classification model (87.1/87.9 F1) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      cwm_generation_pass_f1: 84.3\n      cwm_generation_fail_f1: 85.1\n      cwm_generation_overall_accuracy: 0.847\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_pass_f1: 2.8\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_fail_f1: 2.8\n      cwm_token_budget_overflow_rate: 0.03\n      cwm_exact_match_rate: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      Function-level test 的 expected output 通常很短（单个返回值、True/False、短字符串），\n      token-budget exhaustion 在 CWM debugging 论文中报告的问题主要出现在 repo-level 长 trace 场景。\n      4B 模型在 function-level 生成短输出时不会遇到严重的 token 限制，\n      string-value prediction error 也因输出简单而低频（overflow rate ~3%）。\n      因此 generation 与 classification 的差距被压缩到 ≤4 F1 点，\n      说明 \"task reformulation\" 的优势在 function-level 尺度上不显著——\n      classification 之所以更好，仅仅是因为输出空间更小，而非根本性的 formulation 优势。\n      exact match ~61% 看似不高，但 pass/fail 判定只需对 output 做二值判断，\n      大部分 non-exact-match 的 output 仍能正确推导出 pass/fail 结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Classification vs CWM Generation (Qwen3-4B, function-level)\"\n        columns: [Model, Formulation, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Accuracy, Token_Overflow_Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B-LoRA, Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 0.875, \"N/A\"]\n          - [Qwen3-4B-LoRA, \"CWM Generation\", 84.3, 85.1, 0.847, 0.03]\n          - [Delta, \"\", -2.8, -2.8, -0.028, \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-class F1 bar chart: classification vs generation, 误差棒重叠显著，gap 不具统计显著性 (p>0.05, bootstrap CI)\"\n    analysis: >\n      2.8 F1 的差距在统计上不显著（bootstrap 95% CI 横跨零点）。\n      function-level output 足够短，generation 不遭遇 CWM 论文中的 token-budget 瓶颈。\n      这意味着 \"reformulation from generation to classification\" 的叙事在 function-level 不成立——\n      classification 仅是 marginally better，无法支撑 Claim 1 的核心论点。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B/8B 先生成 execution trace，再从 trace 中抽取 pass/fail。\n      隔离 classification advantage 是来自 formulation（不需要 trace）还是 task simplicity。\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_4b_pass_f1: 85.2\n      ttj_4b_fail_f1: 85.9\n      ttj_8b_pass_f1: 87.8\n      ttj_8b_fail_f1: 88.4\n      ttj_4b_vs_direct_classification_gap: -1.9\n      ttj_8b_vs_direct_classification_gap: 0.7\n      trace_generation_accuracy: 0.78\n      trace_to_verdict_accuracy_given_correct_trace: 0.97\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 在 4B 时略低于 direct classification（-1.9 F1），\n      但在 8B 时反超（+0.7 F1）。这说明 trace generation 确实提供了中间推理步骤的价值，\n      只是 4B 模型容量不足以同时 generate trace 并做 judgment。\n      8B 反超意味着 classification formulation 的优势不是根本性的，\n      而仅仅是 4B 规模下的 capacity 约束造成的——\n      给足参数后，generation + extraction 方案同样有效甚至更好。\n      这直接摧毁了 \"classification is fundamentally simpler\" 的论点：\n      它只是对小模型更友好，不是一个 formulation-level insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification\"\n        columns: [Model, Method, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Avg_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Direct Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5]\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Trace-then-Judge, 85.2, 85.9, 85.6]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Direct Classification, 89.4, 90.1, 89.8]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Trace-then-Judge, 87.8, 88.4, 88.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4B vs 8B 两组对比图，8B 组中 Trace-then-Judge 与 Direct Classification 的 CI 完全重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      TTJ 8B 与 direct classification 8B 差距 <2 F1，且 TTJ 8B 与 direct classification 4B 性能相当。\n      这表明 trace generation 不是瓶颈——模型规模才是。\n      Claim 1 的 \"formulation matters\" 论点被 confound 于 model capacity，无法独立成立。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-level Finetuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved 分类器，\n      隔离 granularity effect vs formulation effect。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_level_accuracy: 0.852\n      traj_level_resolved_f1: 84.8\n      traj_level_unresolved_f1: 85.5\n      per_test_aggregated_to_traj_accuracy: 0.861\n      per_test_vs_traj_level_gap: 0.9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level finetuned 模型直接从 (code, full_test_suite) 预测 resolved/unresolved，\n      不需要 per-test 中间步骤。在 T=1 dominant (68.7%) 的分布下，\n      trajectory-level 与 per-test-then-aggregate 的信息量几乎等价。\n      差距仅 0.9 ppt 说明 per-test granularity 在当前 benchmark 分布下\n      几乎不提供额外信息——aggregation 的理论优势被 T=1 dominance 抹平。\n      少量 T≥2 instances 上 per-test 有优势，但被 T=1 的等价性稀释。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-test Aggregated vs Trajectory-level (Qwen3-4B)\"\n        columns: [Granularity, Accuracy, Resolved_F1, Unresolved_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Per-test → Aggregate, 0.861, 85.7, 86.4]\n          - [Trajectory-level Direct, 0.852, 84.8, 85.5]\n          - [Delta, +0.009, +0.9, +0.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy 对比柱状图，差异在 error bar 内不显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test → aggregate 方法比 trajectory-level 仅高 0.9 ppt，\n      在 bootstrap test 下 p=0.18，不显著。\n      对于 68.7% 的 T=1 instances 而言两种方法数学等价，\n      per-test granularity 的优势仅在 T≥2 的 31.3% 子集上可能体现，\n      但被整体 accuracy 稀释到不可区分。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B→8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM generation 分别 scale 到 8B，\n      观察 classification advantage 是否随规模保持。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_8b_pass_f1: 89.4\n      classification_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cwm_generation_8b_pass_f1: 88.1\n      cwm_generation_8b_fail_f1: 88.7\n      gap_8b: 1.3\n      gap_4b: 2.8\n      gap_trend: \"narrowing\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 规模下 CWM generation 进一步逼近 classification（gap 从 2.8 缩小到 1.3）。\n      更大模型的 generation capacity 提升更快——\n      generation 的难度主要来自需要\"记住\"输出格式和预测具体值，\n      这些随参数量增加而快速改善。\n      Classification 的提升相对 moderate 因为 4B 已接近 function-level 的 ceiling。\n      gap narrowing 趋势进一步削弱 \"formulation advantage\" 论点——\n      如果差距随 scale 消失，那 classification 只是小模型的 regularization effect，\n      不是一个 scale-invariant insight。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Classification vs Generation across Model Sizes\"\n        columns: [Size, Classification_Avg_F1, Generation_Avg_F1, Gap]\n        rows:\n          - [4B, 87.5, 84.7, 2.8]\n          - [8B, 89.8, 88.4, 1.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scaling curve: x=model size, y=avg F1, 两条线收敛\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 从 4B 的 2.8 缩小到 8B 的 1.3，趋势线外推到 ~14B 处交叉。\n      这意味着 classification advantage 是 small-model phenomenon，\n      不是一个 fundamental formulation insight。\n      论文若以此为 main claim 将面临 \"just use a bigger model\" 的 reviewer 质疑。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      200 instances 上比较：repair agent 使用 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，\n      衡量 resolve rate lift。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 0.34\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.345\n      resolve_rate_lift_pct: 0.5\n      diagnostic_precision_at_threshold: 0.69\n      actionable_diagnostic_rate: 0.23\n    result_rationale: >\n      Diagnostic re-repair 要求两个条件同时满足：(1) per-test prediction 足够准确以识别 failing test，\n      (2) repair agent 能利用 \"test X fails\" 信息生成 targeted fix。\n      在 worst 档位下，per-test failure precision 仅 0.69，意味着 ~31% 的诊断指向是错误的，\n      给 repair agent 引入噪声反而可能 mislead。\n      此外，即使诊断正确，repair agent 可能已经从 error message 中获得等价信息，\n      使得 per-test prediction 的边际信息量很低。\n      0.5% lift 在 200 instances 上对应 ~1 个额外 resolved instance，\n      远低于统计显著性门槛。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Resolve Rates\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve_Rate, N_Resolved, Lift]\n        rows:\n          - [No diagnostic, 0.340, \"68/200\", \"—\"]\n          - [With per-test diagnostic, 0.345, \"69/200\", \"+0.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Resolve rate 柱状图，error bar 完全重叠\"\n      - \"Error analysis: 诊断正确且 repair 成功 vs 诊断错误且 mislead 的 case breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      0.5% lift 不显著（Fisher exact test p=0.91）。\n      定性分析显示：诊断正确的 cases 中，repair agent 在无诊断条件下也多数能 resolve（从 error trace 获得等价信息）；\n      诊断错误的 cases 中，misleading 信息反而导致 repair agent 走偏。\n      净效果接近零。Claim 2 不成立。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Failure Precision/Recall\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall。\n    expected_results:\n      per_test_failure_precision: 0.71\n      per_test_failure_recall: 0.65\n      per_test_failure_f1: 0.679\n      per_test_pass_precision: 0.89\n      per_test_pass_recall: 0.92\n      false_positive_rate: 0.08\n      false_negative_rate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Failure 是少数类（~35% of test outcomes in training data），precision/recall 偏低是预期的。\n      模型对 PASS 的预测更可靠（recall 0.92）因为 PASS 是多数类且模式更 regular。\n      FAIL prediction 的 35% false negative rate 意味着模型漏掉了 1/3 的真实 failure，\n      这直接限制了 diagnostic signal 的下游可用性——\n      如果你只能捕获 65% 的 failing tests，剩余 35% 的遗漏会让 repair agent \n      以为某些 test 是通过的（实际未通过），产生 false confidence。\n      71% precision 意味着每指出的 ~3.5 个 failing test 中有 1 个是误报。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-test Prediction Quality\"\n        columns: [Label, Precision, Recall, F1, Support]\n        rows:\n          - [PASS, 0.89, 0.92, 0.905, \"~6500\"]\n          - [FAIL, 0.71, 0.65, 0.679, \"~3500\"]\n          - [Macro Avg, 0.80, 0.785, 0.792, \"~10000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for FAIL class，AUC-PR ~0.72\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap\"\n    analysis: >\n      FAIL class 的 F1=0.679 处于 worst 定义范围内。\n      与 overall accuracy 0.875 的落差说明 class imbalance 下 per-test failure detection 困难。\n      这个精度水平不足以支撑可靠的 diagnostic feedback——\n      下游 re-repair 实验中 0.5% lift 的结果与此一致。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T=3+) 分层的 oracle advantage 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct: 0.687\n      T1_iid_adv: 0.0\n      T1_block_adv: 0.0\n      T2_pct: 0.158\n      T2_iid_adv: 0.042\n      T2_block_adv: 0.118\n      T3plus_pct: 0.155\n      T3plus_iid_adv: 0.185\n      T3plus_block_adv: 0.362\n      weighted_avg_iid_adv: 0.035\n      weighted_avg_block_adv: 0.075\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=1 时 per-test 与 trajectory-level 数学等价（advantage = 0）。\n      T=2 时 iid advantage 仅 0.042 因为两个独立 coin flips 的组合增益很小。\n      T=3+ 时 advantage 显著（iid 0.185, block 0.362），但仅占 15.5% instances。\n      加权平均后 iid advantage 仅 0.035, block 仅 0.075——\n      在 worst 档下 block correlation 未被实证支持，\n      所以实际 expected advantage 接近 iid 的 0.035，\n      即 per-test 在当前 SWE-bench 分布下仅贡献 ~3.5 ppt 的 oracle advantage。\n      这个 3.5 ppt 还是 oracle 上界——实际模型的 advantage 会更小。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Oracle Per-test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [T_stratum, Instance_Pct, iid_Advantage, Block_Advantage]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", 0.000, 0.000]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"15.8%\", 0.042, 0.118]\n          - [\"T=3+\", \"15.5%\", 0.185, 0.362]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", 0.035, 0.075]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: T 分层分布 + 各层 advantage overlay\"\n      - \"Advantage vs T 曲线，标注 SWE-bench T 分布的 CDF\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test advantage 高度集中在 T≥3（仅 15.5% instances），\n      但 SWE-bench 的 T=1 dominance (68.7%) 使加权 advantage 骤降。\n      这是 Claim 3 的核心可回收发现：per-test verification 有价值的严格前提条件\n      在当前主流 benchmark 上不被满足。\n      作为 analysis paper 的贡献有说服力，但作为 method paper 的 motivation 不够。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练模型的 test-level predictions 中测量实际 error correlation 结构，\n      与 iid 和 block-correlated simulation 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_corr_within_instance: 0.06\n      iid_simulation_spearman: 0.02\n      block_simulation_spearman: 0.45\n      observed_closer_to: \"iid\"\n      kendall_tau: 0.04\n      avg_error_cluster_size: 1.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Block correlation 假设（同一 instance 内所有 test 的 prediction error 高度相关）\n      基于直觉：如果模型不理解 patch 的语义，所有 test 都会预测错误。\n      但实际上 4B 模型的错误更 heterogeneous——\n      有些 test 因为 input/output pattern 简单而容易预测正确，\n      即使模型对 patch 语义理解不完整。\n      Spearman 0.06 接近 iid 基线 (0.02) 而远离 block 模拟 (0.45)，\n      说明 errors 近似独立。\n      这意味着 oracle analysis 中 block-correlated 列的数字不适用于实际模型，\n      per-test advantage 应参考 iid 列——进一步缩小 advantage。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [Model, Spearman_ρ, Kendall_τ, Avg_Error_Cluster]\n        rows:\n          - [Observed (Qwen3-4B), 0.06, 0.04, 1.2]\n          - [iid Simulation, 0.02, 0.01, 1.05]\n          - [Block Simulation, 0.45, 0.38, 3.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error correlation heatmap: instances × tests，显示 near-random pattern\"\n      - \"Q-Q plot: observed correlation distribution vs iid null distribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      Observed Spearman ρ=0.06，远低于 block simulation (0.45)，\n      仅略高于 iid (0.02)。KS test 无法拒绝 iid null (p=0.23)。\n      Block correlation assumption 不成立。\n      Oracle analysis 中的 block advantage 列 (0.075 weighted) 不适用，\n      实际应参考 iid advantage 列 (0.035 weighted)。\n      Per-test 的理论优势进一步缩水。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重新评估 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_instances: 412\n      docker_failure_rate: 0.176\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 47.3\n      avg_f2p_tests: 2.1\n      avg_p2p_tests: 45.2\n      total_test_examples: 311072\n      p2p_regression_rate: 0.013\n    result_rationale: >\n      Docker 评估的 ~17.6% 失败率来自环境配置不兼容（依赖版本、Python 版本等），\n      与 SWE-bench 官方 Docker 评估的已知问题一致。\n      412 instances × 16 candidates × avg 47.3 tests ≈ 311K test-level examples。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3% 与之前 p2p-regression-rate 实验结论一致（negative）。\n      这个数据集本身有资源贡献价值，但 per-test labels 在 worst 档下\n      无法驱动比 trajectory-level 显著更好的 verification。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Instances (successful), 412]\n          - [Candidates per instance, 16]\n          - [Avg total tests, 47.3]\n          - [Avg F2P tests, 2.1]\n          - [Avg P2P tests, 45.2]\n          - [P2P regression rate, \"1.3%\"]\n          - [Total test examples, \"~311K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"F2P test count 分布直方图，长尾但中位数=1\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功但统计特性与 function-level 类似：F2P 中位数=1，T=1 dominant。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3% 低于 oracle study 中 10% 阈值，\n      确认 P2P tests 在当前 benchmark 上不提供有用的 verification signal。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-level Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B/8B fine-tune on repo-level (patched_code, test_code) → pass/fail。\n    expected_results:\n      repo_4b_pass_f1: 62.1\n      repo_4b_fail_f1: 59.7\n      repo_4b_accuracy: 0.643\n      repo_8b_pass_f1: 67.3\n      repo_8b_fail_f1: 65.8\n      repo_8b_accuracy: 0.689\n      context_length_avg_tokens: 6200\n      context_truncation_rate: 0.31\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level test code 远长于 function-level（avg 6200 tokens vs ~800），\n      且 patched code 包含跨文件修改，语义复杂度远高于单函数。\n      4B 模型 context window 限制导致 31% instances 需要 truncation，\n      严重损害 prediction quality。\n      62/60 F1 远低于 function-level 的 87/88，\n      也低于 repo-level per_class_f1 worst 范围上界 69。\n      8B 通过更大 context capacity 部分缓解 truncation，\n      但 67/66 F1 仍不足以在实践中竞争 execution-based verification。\n      这个 accuracy 水平下的 per-test diagnostic 几乎无意义——\n      模型对 repo-level code 的理解不足以可靠区分 pass/fail。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Repo-level Classification Results\"\n        columns: [Model, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Accuracy, Truncation_Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B, 62.1, 59.7, 0.643, 0.31]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 67.3, 65.8, 0.689, 0.22]\n          - [\"Function-level 4B (ref)\", 87.1, 87.9, 0.875, 0.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Function-level vs Repo-level accuracy 对比，显示 >20 ppt gap\"\n      - \"Accuracy vs context length scatter，truncation 区域 accuracy 骤降\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level results 低于 70% F1 (worst 范围)，不具竞争力。\n      Function-level 到 repo-level 的 generalization gap 巨大（>20 ppt），\n      说明 per-test classification 的 function-level 成功不能外推到实际 SE 场景。\n      这强化了 analysis paper 的叙事：方法的适用条件很窄。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge (trajectory-level + per-test)。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_accuracy: 0.71\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_pass_f1: 74.2\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_fail_f1: 68.5\n      qwen3_32b_traj_accuracy: 0.78\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_pass_f1: 80.1\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_fail_f1: 76.3\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_vs_finetuned_4b_gap: -7.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 在 trajectory-level 上表现尚可（32B 达 78%），\n      但 per-test 精度低于 fine-tuned 4B classifier。\n      32B zero-shot per-test avg F1 78.2 vs fine-tuned 4B 87.5，差距 9.3 ppt——\n      说明 fine-tuning 仍有价值，但也表明 32B 的 zero-shot 能力已不差。\n      在 worst 档下这些 baseline 主要的意义是填充 Pareto frontier 图表，\n      显示 cost-accuracy tradeoff 的全貌。\n      但 32B zero-shot trajectory-level 78% 接近 fine-tuned 4B per-test 87.5%，\n      如果考虑 inference cost，zero-shot large model 是一个不错的 alternative——\n      这进一步削弱了 fine-tuned per-test classifier 的独立价值。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines vs Fine-tuned Classifier\"\n        columns: [Model, Method, Traj_Acc, PerTest_Pass_F1, PerTest_Fail_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, Zero-shot, 0.71, 74.2, 68.5]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Zero-shot, 0.78, 80.1, 76.3]\n          - [Qwen3-4B, Fine-tuned, 0.875, 87.1, 87.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier: x=inference cost (FLOPs), y=accuracy，标注各 method\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B 在 Pareto frontier 上优于 zero-shot 32B（更低 cost，更高 accuracy），\n      但这是 fine-tuning vs zero-shot 的一般结论，不是 per-test formulation 的功劳。\n      32B zero-shot trajectory-level 已接近 practical utility threshold。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Classification model 的 per-test majority voting (K=3)。\n    expected_results:\n      k1_pass_f1: 87.1\n      k1_fail_f1: 87.9\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      k3_fail_f1: 88.9\n      k3_lift: 1.1\n      k3_inference_cost_multiplier: 3.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      K=3 majority voting 提供 ~1.1 F1 的 lift，符合 self-consistency 的一般收益规律。\n      但 3x inference cost 换取 1.1 ppt 的 cost-effectiveness 很差。\n      在 worst 档下这个实验主要显示 per-test classification 已接近 \n      function-level 的 accuracy ceiling，additional inference budget 的 marginal return 递减。\n      不改变任何 main claim 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Majority Voting Results (K=3)\"\n        columns: [K, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Cost_Multiplier]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 87.1, 87.9, \"1x\"]\n          - [3, 88.3, 88.9, \"3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K vs F1 曲线，快速饱和\"\n    analysis: >\n      Low-impact experiment。1.1 ppt lift 不改变 worst 档的整体 narrative。\n      可放入 appendix 作为 completeness，不需要在 main paper 中讨论。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"843dc94e-0769-44b6-9749-612cb0b86756","total_cost_usd":0.310017,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10118,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":9427,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10118,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9427,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10118},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5074,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005174000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9427,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10118,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.304843,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b2ee3308-e3d6-48d2-bde6-79ee00559c03"}
